    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] Review 2026-11-01 at dev 100b6fbb6e: fixture binds types.add*(var seq[Tweets]; Tweet) at 0.85 for a field chain (h.photos.add p), an inferred local (var xs = newSeq[Photo]()), a module-level var, and result.add(t) where the second argument decides; the declared-type control goes external. The self-call shape (timeline.add inside add*) never reaches run output: deduplicate_edges(remove_self_loops=True) at cli.py:13189 drops it. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nFOUND 2026-10-04 measuring WI-bivab on nitter 8114eef (branch jgstern-agent/fix/hilum).\n\nWI-bivab's first-argument check reads only DECLARED, PROC-LOCAL types: a proc parameter, `result` (the declared return type) and a `var`/`let`/`const` written with a type before the call. Of the 64 nitter calls that bound `types.add*(timeline: var seq[Tweets]; tweet: Tweet)` on dev, 38 are now left to the library; 26 still bind:\n- 19 field chains (`result.thread.content.add tweet`, `tweet.reply.add name`): the receiver's type is a FIELD's declared type, which the check does not walk;\n- 4 locals whose type is inferred from the initializer (`var replacements = newSeq[ReplaceSlice]()` twice, `var url = decoded(..)`, `var path = req.params.getOrDefault(..)`);\n- 1 MODULE-level typed variable (`sessionPool: seq[Session]` in auth.nim): only proc-local declarations are read;\n- 2 where the receiver type MATCHES and the SECOND argument decides: `result.add(thread)` with `result: seq[Tweets]` and `thread: Tweets` (system add, not `add*(.., tweet: Tweet)`), and the self-call inside `add*` itself (`timeline.add @[tweet]`).\n\nSoundness caveat to carry with any extension: Nim `converter`s make implicit conversions the check assumes impossible; WI-losaf records that converters are not extracted at all, so a repository converter can make an exclusion wrong today. Not measured: how many repositories declare converters on types the check reasons about."  # 4c54
